{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/347578-a-new-game-and-a-new-player","id":347578,"title":"A new game and a new player","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-22T12:13:29-08:00","id":347578,"title":"A new game and a new player","content":"Hello everyone, I just joined this site because I am joining into a new game and I would like some help from players building my character. The last one I made was basically forced out because he broke an oath to his king because he wouldn't murder normal humans. And this caused one of the other PCs to refuse to trust him, making a motley impossible. He was a guerilla fighter type character. I am now going to make a mental character but I honestly have no idea how to make that type of character in Changeling as this is my first time playing the game. And the more I go to the DM the more I just want to scream and do it all myself. I was thinking an autumn courtier who basically terrifies everyone, basically reveling in the terror he causes.<br /> <br /> So this game is 1920s Chicago, and prohibition just started. The courts are all basically controlled by the Spring King who is allied with one of the gangs and is moving the Freehold into being more a part of the gang. There is no real story for the PCs yet. I don't know how to make something for the setting or the system so I would welcome any and all help at this point. Maybe even breaking the fuck out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4595-viserack","user":"Viserack","date":". 12-22-2014, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4595-viserack","name":"Viserack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T15:50:38-08:00","id":348601,"title":"","content":"It really depends on what you want out of a &quot;mental&quot; character. A nightmarish Autumn courtier is a good detail to work from, but even then your options are virtually limitless.<br /> <br /> Since you've said you want a character who terrifies everyone, suggesting less of a creepy, unsettling character and more the type to loom and lurk in shadows, only to appear unexpectedly... let me give you a sample character concept of my own based on that idea:<br /> <br /> Beast seeming, either Windwing or Cleareyes kith, based on an owl. (You could dual-kith both of those, or combine one with Hunterheart for the talons!) Dots in Stealth and Intimidation are a must, at least one in Animal Ken and Survival likely. Why is everyone scared of him? Obviously owls are silent night predators who drop down on their prey unexpectedly, but why do other changelings fear him? Is he a relentless bounty hunter for oath-breakers? An infernal occultist skilled in dark magic and curses? A spy, or blackmailer, who makes it his business to know everyone's dirty secrets? Additional dots in Athletics and at least one combat skill, Occult and/or Investigation can be tailored to fit whichever of these concepts you choose.<br /> <br /> Does that help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T03:52:33-08:00","id":353592,"title":"","content":"What kind of terror do you want to casue? Do you want it to cause directly by your presence? Indirectly through actions? After all, there is a difference between a nasty brutish ogre that terrifies people through the threat of violence and a knack for cruelty, a beautiful fairest with a heart of ice that thinks of the most inventive ways to manipulate others into doing dangerous things or that darkling who not only speaks with ghosts but gets them to do things for her such as spying (and then using that lore to blackmail people).<br /> <br /> Anyway, mental character in my campaign that seems to fit the image you are going for is a wizened/brewmaster with a voodoo priest background. He is working on the beast contract and then take a pet boa constrictor He went for a more white voodoo type of character with the Spring Court and a focus on healing, but with a minor twist you have the black witch with a knack for poison and contacts with some of the more dark elements of supernatural sorcery (in my campaign the vampires of Miami are dominated by the Crone and Voodoo practices). We are both looking at adapting the blood magic of the Circle of the Crone into a kind of alchemy/brewing type of contract including goblin fruit recipees to replace the blood magic spells. Mind you, that is still just an idea so no practical advice in that regards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}